<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parliament of Great Britain</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1707–1800</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Parliament of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a> was the legislature of the Kingdom of Great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, formed in 1707 by the union of the parliaments of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and meeting at Westminster. By the Declaratory Act of 1720 it claimed the right to legislate for Ireland, a claim given up in 1782–1783. It was replaced in 1801 by the Parliament of the United Kingdom.</p></div>
